    id: "default-pdf-creator",
    name: "pdf-creator",
    description: "Creates professional, accessible, well-structured PDF documents from user requirements or source material. Use for reports, guides, proposals, handouts, forms, and document exports.",
    skillFile: "SKILL.md",
    skillContent: "---\nname: pdf-creator\ndescription: \"Creates professional, accessible, well-structured PDF documents from user requirements or source material. Use for reports, guides, proposals, handouts, forms, and document exports.\"\n---\n# PDF Creator\n\n## Mission\nProduce polished, readable, correctly structured PDF files whose content is accurate and whose layout survives export and printing.\n\n## Workflow\n1. **Determine requirements**\n   - Identify purpose, audience, page size, orientation, branding, language, accessibility needs, and whether the PDF must be editable, fillable, or print-ready.\n   - Determine whether content should be authored, transformed from source material, or preserved verbatim.\n2. **Prepare content**\n   - Create a logical hierarchy with title, sections, headings, captions, tables, references, and appendices as needed.\n   - Preserve meaning, figures, dates, units, and citations from source material.\n   - Flag missing information instead of inventing it.\n3. **Choose production method**\n   - Use a document-first layout workflow for text-heavy reports.\n   - Use vector elements for crisp diagrams and charts; use raster images only when appropriate.\n   - Embed fonts where licensing permits and use fonts with required language glyph coverage.\n   - Use semantic structure and tagged PDF features when the toolchain supports them.\n4. **Design**\n   - Apply consistent typography, spacing, margins, headers/footers, page numbers, and color.\n   - Keep tables readable and prevent awkward splits, clipped text, and orphaned headings.\n   - Add alt text or accessible equivalents for meaningful visuals where supported.\n   - Ensure contrast and do not rely on color alone.\n5. **Generate and inspect**\n   - Export the PDF.\n   - Render or inspect every page, not just the first page.\n   - Check page count, text extraction, links, fonts, images, table boundaries, and special characters.\n   - Fix overflow, blank pages, broken glyphs, and inconsistent spacing.\n6. **Deliver**\n   - Provide the file and a short description of its contents.\n   - State whether it is tagged, fillable, editable, or print-ready only when verified.\n\n## Quality checklist\n- [ ] All requested content is present and accurate.\n- [ ] Page size and orientation are correct.\n- [ ] Typography and spacing are consistent.\n- [ ] No clipping, overlap, overflow, or unintended blank pages.\n- [ ] Tables and images are legible.\n- [ ] Fonts and special characters render correctly.\n- [ ] Links and page numbering work.\n- [ ] Accessibility features are described accurately.\n- [ ] Final exported PDF was inspected.\n\n## Content and rights\n- Preserve source citations and attribution.\n- Do not fabricate references, signatures, certifications, or official seals.\n- Do not reproduce copyrighted source material beyond what the user is authorized to use.\n- Treat sensitive personal information carefully and include only what is needed.\n",
    files: [],
